  "prefLabel": "Juv 301.05 Notice of Right to Counsel Parole Revocation Proceedings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Juv 301.05 Notice of Right to Counsel Parole Revocation Proceedings. For juveniles subject to parole revocation proceedings, effective notice of the right to counsel and notice of statutory requirements regarding waiver of the right to counsel, shall be provided in a written notice by the juvenile parole board at the time of the preliminary hearing, to be held no less than 3 business prior to parole revocation proceedings.\n\nSource. #14223, eff 3-28-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/juv100-400.html"
}
